Summary: Rewrite binds to 127.x.x.x addresses macOS refuses, for GOG Galaxy
Category: system
Kind: workaround
Origin: crossover
From: CrossOver 26.3.0 (same code as 25.1.1) CW HACK 24472
Source: https://media.codeweavers.com/pub/crossover/source/crossover-sources-25.1.1.tar.gz (sources/wine/server/sock.c)
CW-Hack: 24472
Upstream: no
Why: macOS only lets sockets bind to 127.0.0.1 among the 127/8 addresses; rewrite other 127.x.x.x binds so GOG Galaxy can start.
Evidence: Sikarugir 10.0_8: wineserver: 'HACK: rewriting bind loopback address to 127.0.0.1'.
Port: unchanged from 10.0 (applies with offsets); CX 26.3.0's server/sock.c has the
 identical hunk.
Applies to: wine 11.22

diff --git a/server/sock.c b/server/sock.c
index 93505d5..360fe02 100644
--- a/server/sock.c
+++ b/server/sock.c
@@ -3051,6 +3051,18 @@ static void sock_ioctl( struct fd *fd, ioctl_code_t code, struct async *async )
 
         if (unix_addr.addr.sa_family == AF_INET)
         {
+#if defined(__APPLE__)
+            /* CW Hack 24472. macOS does not support binding to any loopback
+             * address other than 127.0.0.1. This is an incomplete and incorrect
+             * rewrite, but it's enough to satisfy GOG Galaxy. */
+            if ((unix_addr.in.sin_addr.s_addr & 0xff) == 127 &&
+                unix_addr.in.sin_addr.s_addr != htonl( INADDR_LOOPBACK ))
+            {
+                fprintf(stderr, "HACK: rewriting bind loopback address to 127.0.0.1\n");
+                bind_addr.in.sin_addr.s_addr = htonl( INADDR_LOOPBACK );
+            }
+#endif
+
             if (!memcmp( &unix_addr.in.sin_addr, magic_loopback_addr, 4 )
                     || bind_to_interface( sock, &unix_addr.in ))
                 bind_addr.in.sin_addr.s_addr = htonl( INADDR_ANY );
